WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.201
-In one of the most
chilling moments

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.236
of his presidency --

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.303
and there have been a few --

00:00:04.303 --> 00:00:05.871
Donald Trump refused to commit

00:00:05.871 --> 00:00:07.841
to a peaceful
transition of power

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.442
as Republicans formulated a plan

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.310
to steal the election
through the courts.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.680
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.983
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:20.553
We're as close as we've ever
been to losing our democracy

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.121
and watching our
government transform

00:00:22.121 --> 00:00:23.790
into a autocratic regime.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.658
It's happening right in front
of our eyes, right now.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:29.194
You don't need to wait for Trump
to roll down Pennsylvania Avenue

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:32.431
on a tank and green fatigues
with a long chin beard,

00:00:32.431 --> 00:00:34.567
especially since,
if he did try to grow one,

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.169
he'd probably just look like
a very sick Chihuahua.

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:38.704
"I think my dog is dying."

00:00:38.704 --> 00:00:40.039
Is he drinking water?

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:40.973
"No, just like Diet Coke,

00:00:40.973 --> 00:00:43.542
like ten, ten a day."

00:00:43.542 --> 00:00:45.678
The president's falsely claiming
the election is rigged.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.947
The GOP chair in Pennsylvania
told The Atlantic --

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:50.816
on the record --
that they're considering a plan

00:00:50.816 --> 00:00:53.152
to steal the state's
electoral votes, if they lose,

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:56.155
and Republicans are basically
announcing their intention

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:59.091
to use the courts to overturn
the election results.

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:01.127
And, on top of all that,
the president, last night,

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:03.796
refused to commit to a peaceful
transfer of power,

00:01:03.796 --> 00:01:05.364
effectively
threatening violence,

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.199
unless ballots are thrown out

00:01:07.199 --> 00:01:08.668
and he's allowed
to stay in office.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:15.541 line:0%
-Well, we're gonna have
to see what happens.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:17.710 line:0%
You know that I've been
complaining very strongly

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.047 line:0%
about the ballots
and the ballots are a disaster.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:24.817 line:0%
Alright. I know.

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.419 line:0%
No, we wanna have --

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.120 line:0%
We wanna have --
Get rid of the ballots

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.188
and you'll have a very transf--

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:30.823
We'll have a very peaceful --

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:32.392
There won't be
a transfer, frankly.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:34.027
There'll be a continuation.

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:35.461
-Alright, I'll take it back.

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:37.697
He probably will grow
that dictator beard.

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.865
[ As Trump ]
Do you like it?
I comb it with a fork.

00:01:39.865 --> 00:01:41.901
It's a little pasta twirl.

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:43.436
So, Trump is
threatening violence,

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.037
unless we
"get rid of the ballots."

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:47.941
He's threatening a coup d'état,
even though I'm sure he has

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:49.842
no idea what the phrase
coup d'état means.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:52.412 line:0%
He probably thinks it's
a lyric from "Moulin Rouge!"

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.345
[ As Trump ]
♪ Voulez vous coucher ♪

00:01:53.345 --> 00:01:54.547
♪ Coup d'état ♪

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:55.548
♪ Ce soir? ♪

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:56.916
[ Laughing ]
We're in a --

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.719
a truly treacherous moment,

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.788
yet, we can still enjoy
a "Moulin Rouge!" joke.

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:04.456
Our democracy hasn't been
healthy in a long time,

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:06.258
but, now,
it's in a death spiral.

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:08.627
The president is threatening
violence, if he loses.

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:10.863
Armed right-wing militias
are roaming the streets

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:12.866 line:0%
in Louisville,
intimidating protesters.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.066 line:0%
The president is glorifying

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:15.735 line:0%
state violence
against journalists.

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.336 line:0%
Just a few months ago,
he called for

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:19.539 line:0%
overwhelming force
to suppress protests,

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:22.174 line:0%
labeled democratic cities
"anarchist jurisdictions,"

00:02:22.174 --> 00:02:24.811 line:0%
and his campaign called
for an army of supporters

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.946
to join an election
security squad.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:28.447
If this were happening
in any other country,

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:30.917
you'd expect to see
pro-regime militants

00:02:30.917 --> 00:02:32.819
driving through the streets
in pickup trucks,

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.820
attacking people
and waving flags and --

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:37.023
Ah, goddamn it!

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:38.524
The only thing missing
from that clip

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:41.361
is a foreign correspondent
for the BBC in a flak jacket.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:42.996
[ English accent ]
The scene here is tense

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:45.631
as pro-regime forces
clash with dissidents.

00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:47.233
And I am sorry.
I'm just getting word

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:50.903
the regime has sent its armada
of Jet Skis and party boats

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:53.539
to blockade the port,
leaving nothing in their wake

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:56.142
but empty aluminium cans
of Natural Light

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.578
or, as it's called
in the local vernacular,

00:02:58.578 --> 00:02:59.912
Natty Light.

00:02:59.912 --> 00:03:03.615
Yes, we did go well out
of our way to say aluminium.

00:03:03.615 --> 00:03:05.618
But don't worry.
Don't worry, guys.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:08.153
The White House press corps
is ready to step in

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:10.556
to its role as the guardian
of democracy

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.792
in this perilous moment
for the republic.

00:03:12.792 --> 00:03:16.295
-Prince Harry and Meghan Markle
chimed in on the US election

00:03:16.295 --> 00:03:17.429
and essentially
encouraged people

00:03:17.429 --> 00:03:19.332
to vote for Joe Biden.

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.566
I wanted to get
your reaction to that.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.234
-Mm, I don't have my glasses on.

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.470
Was that Woodward or Bernstein?

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.405
Does US Weekly have
a White House correspondent?

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:27.906
Although, I bet even
US Weekly would drop

00:03:27.906 --> 00:03:29.676
its Harry and Meghan
coverage for this...

00:03:30.977 --> 00:03:32.278
Seriously,
if the president threatens

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.546
to destroy American democracy

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.947
by seizing power
through violence,

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:37.583
maybe scrap your preplanned
question about Harry and Meghan.

00:03:37.583 --> 00:03:39.518
You need to be able to,
you know, pivot on the fly.

00:03:39.518 --> 00:03:40.987
What if, at his next
press conference,

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:43.823
Trump takes out the red button
and threatens to nuke Seattle,

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.791
unless they give him $1 billion?

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.126
"Sir, I'd love to hear more
of your thoughts

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.327
about nuking Seattle, but,

00:03:48.327 --> 00:03:49.962
"Keeping Up with the
Kardashians" is ending.

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:51.864
Do you have a comment on that?"
And I gotta ask,

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.634
why aren't more
elected Democrats

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:57.836
acting like this
is the emergency it is?

00:03:57.836 --> 00:03:59.071
They're about as effective

00:03:59.071 --> 00:04:01.173
as the receptionist
on "Law &amp; Order" who says,

00:04:01.173 --> 00:04:04.176
"Hey, you can't go in there!"
while they're going in there.

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:05.811
Democrats should be grinding
the gears of government

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:07.580
to a halt
until the Republican Party

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.381
vows to respect
the election outcome

00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:11.717
and commit to a peaceful
transition of power.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:15.554
They should be holding public
televised hearings about this.

00:04:15.554 --> 00:04:18.557
The only person I've heard talk
about it is Bernie Sanders.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.326 line:0%
-What do we do if Trump loses

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.061 line:0%
and he won't leave office?

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.629 line:0%
-What we have got to do is work

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:25.030 line:0%
in a number of ways

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.433 line:0%
and one of the ways is --

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.402 line:0%
I'm working on this
right now --

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:32.004 line:0%
is to demand that both
the House and the Senate

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:35.875 line:0%
hold hearings, right now!

00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.677 line:0%
To educate the American people

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.579 line:0%
about what might happen

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:41.914 line:0%
and to develop
antidotes to that.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.450 line:0%
So we've got to educate
the American people

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.652 line:0%
about what is in front of us

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:50.523 line:0%
and rally the American people
to tell Donald Trump

00:04:50.523 --> 00:04:52.058 line:0%
that too many people
in this country

00:04:52.058 --> 00:04:55.494 line:0%
have fought and died
to defend American democracy

00:04:55.494 --> 00:04:57.496 line:0%
and, if and when you lose,

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:59.432 line:0%
you're getting out of office.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.700
-The best part of any Bernie
interview during the pandemic

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:02.868
are his Zoom backgrounds.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.002
It's like when you use

00:05:04.002 --> 00:05:05.638
the computer
at your grandparents' house

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:08.507
and their desktop still has the
default background from Windows.

00:05:08.507 --> 00:05:12.445
His background always look like
the cover of a nature sounds CD.

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:14.380
[ As Sanders ]
Birds singing,
crickets chirping,

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.148
the sound of a babbling brook

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:18.417
as you gently
drift off to sleep.

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:20.285
Now, go to sleep! CD over!
I got work to do.

00:05:20.285 --> 00:05:22.621
But he's absolutely right --
Democrats should be holding

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:24.490
highly publicized hearings
about this.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.793
They should be slowing down
Senate business,

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.760
doing everything possible
to force Republicans

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.396
to commit to honor
the results of the election

00:05:31.396 --> 00:05:33.065
because Trump clearly will not.

00:05:33.065 --> 00:05:35.334
He said as much repeatedly
over the last few weeks

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.604
and, yet, we all just kind of
sigh and move on with our lives.

00:05:38.604 --> 00:05:39.972
Whenever he screams

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:42.808
something about mail-in ballots
or a rigged election,

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:43.909
we're all like tourists

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:46.112
rolling up our car windows
in Times Square.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.246
"Honey, uh, quick.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:48.481
Quick, Buzz Lightyear's
coming this way

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.416
and, for some reason,
he has a giant sword?"

00:05:50.416 --> 00:05:53.418
But Trump has made it
very clear, for months now,

00:05:53.418 --> 00:05:55.687
that he will not consider
the election legitimate

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:58.057
if he loses,
based on his made-up claims

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.558
of mail-in voting fraud.

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:01.960
-Universal is going
to be a disaster

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:05.197
the likes of which
our country has never seen.

00:06:05.197 --> 00:06:06.865
It'll end up being
a rigged election

00:06:06.865 --> 00:06:08.901
or they will never come out
with an outcome.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.270
They'll have to do it again.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.572
And nobody wants that
and I don't want that.

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:15.074
You won't know
the election result

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:17.710
for weeks, months,
maybe years after.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.579
Maybe you'll never know
the election result,

00:06:19.579 --> 00:06:21.213
and that's what
I'm concerned with.

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:23.282
It'll be fixed.
It'll be rigged.

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.717
People oughta get smart.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:27.186
It'll be the greatest
rigged election in history.

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:30.323
It'll be the greatest fraud
ever perpetrated.

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:31.657 line:0%
The only way

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.492 line:0%
we're gonna lose this election

00:06:33.492 --> 00:06:35.461 line:0%
is if the election is rigged.

00:06:35.461 --> 00:06:37.296 line:0%
Remember that.
It's the only way

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.830 line:0%
we're gonna lose this election.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.099
-You think "the only way"

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.300
you could possibly lose
is if it's rigged?

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.804
You haven't cracked 50%
in the polling average all year.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:47.372
That's like K.Fed
saying the only reason

00:06:47.372 --> 00:06:49.074
his album didn't go platinum
was because

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:52.111
the Billboard charts were rigged
against "PopoZao."

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:54.714
[ As Federline ]
We love "PopoZao,"
don't we, folks?

00:06:54.714 --> 00:06:57.183
You're hearing it more and more.

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.017
You haven't a been
ahead of Biden in the
polling average once.

00:06:59.017 --> 00:07:00.853
You lost the popular vote
by three million

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.988
and your approval numbers
have been underwater

00:07:02.988 --> 00:07:04.390
since you launched
your campaign.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:08.294
You're not even at 100%
among Trumps.

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.129
You're even lagging
among old people in Florida.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.697
That's your key constituency.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.732
You are an old person
in Florida.

00:07:13.732 --> 00:07:15.801
That's like Hoda and Jenna
finding out

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:17.002
they're losing the key demo

00:07:17.002 --> 00:07:18.771
of stay-at-home
wine enthusiasts.

00:07:18.771 --> 00:07:21.874
And, yet, Trump keeps insisting
that states are sending

00:07:21.874 --> 00:07:23.909
unsolicited mail ballots
to everyone,

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:26.145
that could easily be
filled out fraudulently,

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:28.748
despite the fact that this
basically never happens

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.650
and would be very easy
to detect.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.852 line:0%
-When you see them cheating
with those ballots,

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:35.221 line:0%
all of those
unsolicited ballots,

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.290 line:0%
those millions of ballots,
you see 'em,

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:40.092 line:0%
anytime you do report 'em
to the authorities.

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:42.194 line:0%
The authorities are
waiting and watching.

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:43.863
-First of all,
they're not unsolicited.

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:46.465
They're ballots. They send them
to registered voters.

00:07:46.465 --> 00:07:48.467
They're not AOL trial CDs.

00:07:48.467 --> 00:07:50.203
[ As Federline ]
Yo, AOL bless.

00:07:50.203 --> 00:07:52.805
Mind if I slip
a "PopoZao" in there?

00:07:52.805 --> 00:07:55.741
I'm having some [ Laughing ]
distribution issues.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.076
We thought it was very,
very important

00:07:58.076 --> 00:08:02.581
to do a lot of comedy today
about 2006's "PopoZao."

00:08:02.581 --> 00:08:05.217
Which is -- I looked at it --
it's a lyric.

00:08:05.217 --> 00:08:07.620
In Portuguese, it means,

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.788
"Bring your ass on the floor

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:12.190
and move it real fast."

00:08:12.190 --> 00:08:15.361
Guy was trying to do like
a nice Rosetta Stone to music.

00:08:15.361 --> 00:08:18.230
Here I am, [ Laughing ]
giving him a hard time.

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.866
I'm assuming that it meant
the dance floor

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:23.435
and not the Senate floor.

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:24.670
[ As McConnell ]
We oughta --

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.806
as soon as we got
that nominee from Donald Trump,

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:28.140
we oughta PopoZao.

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:29.742
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.742 --> 00:08:31.544
[ As Graham ]
I love -- I would love to --

00:08:31.544 --> 00:08:32.411
[ As McConnell ]
Not you, Lindsay.

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:35.814
[ Laughter ]

00:08:35.814 --> 00:08:37.082
Second, Donald Trump --

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:38.150
[ Laughing ] that's who
we were talking about --

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:41.119
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.119 --> 00:08:43.722
[ As McConnell ]
We oughta PopoZao posthaste.

00:08:43.722 --> 00:08:45.124
Please, don't tell
your supporters

00:08:45.124 --> 00:08:46.591
to report anything
to the authorities.

00:08:46.591 --> 00:08:48.761
The last thing we need is
crazed Trump supporters

00:08:48.761 --> 00:08:51.297
sifting through our mail,
looking for fraudulent ballots.

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:52.865
"This has foreign writing on it!

00:08:52.865 --> 00:08:54.166
This is a fraudulent ballot!"

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.968
Sir, that is
an Italian takeout menu.

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:58.404
"Yeah, but who are they
takin' out?

00:08:58.404 --> 00:08:59.738
Answer me that!"

00:08:59.738 --> 00:09:03.175
And, now, Trump is telegraphing
that, if he gets his way

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:06.445
and installs a new Supreme Court
justice before the election,

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:08.547
the conservative
6-3 super majority

00:09:08.547 --> 00:09:10.650
will invalidate
all those ballots

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.951
and declare him the winner,
even if he loses.

00:09:12.951 --> 00:09:17.156
-I think having a 4-4 situation
is not a good situation.

00:09:17.156 --> 00:09:19.758
Now, we're counting
on the federal court system

00:09:19.758 --> 00:09:22.161
to make it so that we
can actually have an evening

00:09:22.161 --> 00:09:24.096
where we know who wins, okay?

00:09:24.096 --> 00:09:25.698
Not where the votes
are gonna be counted

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:27.632
a week later or two weeks later.

00:09:27.632 --> 00:09:30.235
We need nine justices.

00:09:30.235 --> 00:09:31.870
You need that.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:35.107
With the unsolicited millions

00:09:35.107 --> 00:09:37.142
of ballots that they're sending,

